[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "Preamble — Parties and agreement date",
    "text": "AGREEMENT made as of this 29\" day of December, 2006 by and between Prestwick KJ, LLC (hereinafter \"Principal\") and HOKANSON COMPANIES, INC., an Indiana Corporation (hereinafter \"Managing Agent\")."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "1. Appointment, property, and term",
    "text": "1. The Principal hereby appoints the Managing Agent as its exclusive representative, manager and agent for the management of the property located at 5230 and 5250 Bast U.S. Highway 36 (hereinafter, collectively \"Buildings\" in the Town of Danville, State of Indiana, for a period of approximately one (1) year and cight (8) months commencing on March 23, 2006, and ending at midnight on December 31, 2007, and the Managing Agent hereby accepts the appointment."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "2(a). Management duties and standard",
    "text": "(a) Manage the Buildings in the best interest of the Principal, supervise the persons employed in the operation and maintenance of the Buildings and perform such other duties that are customarily performed by Managing Agents. The Manager shall efficiently and economically manage the Buildings and shall do so in a manner equal to the standard of competent office building managers in the Indianapolis greater metropolitan area,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "2(b). Collection of rents and receivables",
    "text": "(b) Use due diligence in the collection of rents and other receivables as they become due."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "2(c). Supplies, repairs, discounts, and charges",
    "text": "(c) Contract for favorable terms, quality and service considered, for supplies, materials, alterations and repaits, as required, and give the Principal the benefit of all discounts or savings thereby obtainable and refrain from accepting any commissions or rebates other than those specifically herein agreed upon. The Managing Agent shall, out of the funds available, properly discharge all applicable and undisputed charges, expenses, claims and demands in order that no liens shall attach to the Buildings."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "2(d). Expenditure and contracting limits",
    "text": "(d) Unless authorized by the Principal, except under circumstances which the Managing Agent shall deem to be an emergency, no expense shall be incurred for any alteration, repair or supply in excess of One Thousand and No/100 Doilars ($1,000.00). The Managing Agent shall not be required to have written approval for all reasonable expenditures for fuel, electricity, water, property and payroll taxes, payrolls, and charges under service contracts approved by the Principal, telephone, license and/or inspection fees, Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained herein, Managing Agent shall not be permitted to execute any contract, agreement or other binding obligation upon Principal which has a term in excess of twelve (12) calendar months (and for purposes of this provision, the word “term” shall include any and all options). Contracts and agreements shall be with third parties who are not related to the Managing Agent or any of its principals,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "2(e). Agency account",
    "text": "(d) Deposit in a separate Agency accounts entitled Hokanson Companies, Inc., Agents for Principal, al] monies received from said Buildings and make withdrawals for operation from such account."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "2(f). Accounts, reports, shortfalls, and audit",
    "text": "(e) Keep separate accurate account of receipts and disbursements involved in the management of the Buildings and render to the Principal on or about the 10th day of each month succeeding the current month, a detailed statement of income and expense for that month, and showing any capital expenditures and listing the name of each payee and the amount thereof and such other information as Principal may reasonably request and shall meet with Principal at reasonably requested times. In the event the disbursements shall be in excess of the receipts collected by the Managing Agent, the Principal agrees to pay such excess promptly upon demand of Managing Agent, Such accounts shall be open to inspection by the Principal at all times, and Principal may audit the same."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "2(g). Personnel",
    "text": "(t) The Managing Agent shall provide, at the expense of the Principal as is more specifically provided in Paragraph 3(a), all personnel necessary for the operation and maintenance of the Buildings. All such personnel shall be employees of the Managing Agent or a legal entity controlled by the Managing Agent."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "2(h). Managing office and operating expenses",
    "text": "(g) Maintain at the Managing Agent's expense an office in downtown Indianapolis designated as the office of the Managing Agent. Office supplies, floor plans, any printed forms, advertising and other expenses identified with the Buildings, shall be provided as part of the Building operating expense."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "2(i). Annual estimate",
    "text": "(h) Submit to Principal prior to each calendat year, an estimate of income and expenses in reasonable detail for the ensuing year, which shall be subject to the approval of Principal."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "2(j). Managing Agent indemnity",
    "text": "(i) To indemnify, defend and save the Principal harmless from all liability, including expenses of defense, arising from any action taken or admitted to be taken, by Managing Agent, its officers, employees, agents or representatives, in the negtigent performance of its duties under this Agreement or otherwise relating to, arising out of, or connected with Managing Agent's breach of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "3(a). Compensation and expense reimbursement",
    "text": "(a) To pay the Managing Agent for services performed hereunder in accordance with Exhibit A attached hereto and made a part hereof, and to reimburse the Managing Agent currently for all expenses, including but not limited to, payroll, workmen's compensation insurance and other payroll-related costs, incurred by the Managing Agent in connection with furnishing personnel for the operation and maintenance of the Buildings as provided in Paragraph 2(a). Notwithstanding the foregoing, Principal shall only be obligated for that portion of such expenses incurred in connection with Operation and maintenance of the Buildings, and not for any other project. The Managing Agent shall not, however, be entitled to relmbursement for any portion of its 2 F:\\apps\\idoclsebree\\hokanson\\Kd_LLCMgmtAgrment revi doc 42/20/06 Case 1:13-cv-00254-TWP-DKL Document 1-1 Filed 02/13/13 | Page 3 of 5 PagelD #: 11 (b) (c) (a) (b) (c) overhead expenses (which term shall include payroll expenses for supervisory employees of the Managing Agent and Managing Agent’s bookkeeping and computer systems and phone systems, and any premiums on any insurance carried for its protection or against damage it may cause or sustain in the operation of the Buildings, but shall include any premium on any insurance carried to protect any liability of another legal entity employing the personnel necessary for the operation and maintenance of the Buildings). Por purposes of the monthly accounting due from the Managing Agent to the Principal under the terms of Paragraph 2(c¢), payments due the Managing Agent under the terms of this subparagraph may be deducted from the current month's receipts."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "3(b). Authorized representative",
    "text": "To designate in writing to Managing Agent, the person authorized by Principal to represent Principal in all matters relating to Managing Agent's responsibilities under this Contract. Any decisions made by such authorized person shall be binding on Principal. Principal hereby initially designates in writing John S, Sebree."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "3(c). Liability insurance",
    "text": "The Principal shail carry, at its exponse, liability insurance covering Hability for property damage and personal injury or death arising from the ownership and operation of the Buildings, which insurance shall operate for the benefit of the Principal, as insured, and the Managing Agent as additional Insured, against such claims and liability which may be incurred in the ownership, management and operation of the Buildings. A Certificate of such insurance shall be supplied to Managing Agent. The amount of such insurance shall be such reasonable amount as the Principal shail determine. As used in this subparagraph, the term \"Managing Agent\" will include any legal-entity owned and controlled by the Managing Agent which may be the employer of employees ongaged in the operation and maintenance of the Buildings."
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "4(a). Cooperation and policies",
    "text": "That the Principal.and Managing Agent shall cooperate in all matters for the successful operation of the Buildings, the Principal having the right to designate general policies and the Managing Agent the privilege and obligation of submitting recommendations."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "4(b). Termination upon sale",
    "text": "In the event the Buildings are sold, either party may cancel this Agreement at the end of any calendar month after closing, upon not less than thitly (30) days’ written notice to the other party of such intention."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "4(c). Termination for uncured breach",
    "text": "In addition, notwithstanding anything contained in this Agreement to the contrary, the parties hereto agree that Principal may terminate this Agreement at any time upon thirty (30) days prior written notice to the Managing Agent upon the occurrence of the following event: Managing Agent's breach of this Agreement, which breach is not cured within thirty (30) days after Principal's written notice to Managing Agent advising of such breach (or such longer period of time as is reasonable so long as Managing Agent has commenced to cure and diligently pursuing cure of such breach), but in any event never longer than 90 days."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "5. Successors and assigns",
    "text": "5. This Agreement shall be binding upon the parties hereto, their heirs, executors, administrators, successors and assigns,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "5. Prevailing-party expenses",
    "text": "In the event of any dispute between the parties arising out of, related to or connected with this Agreement, the prevailing party shall be entitled to collect from the non-prevailing party all of its reasonable expenses incurred in connection with such dispute, including but not limited lo reasonable attorneys’ fees and expenses."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "5. Counterparts and signatures",
    "text": "This Agreement may be executed in multiple counterparts cach of which, when taken together, shall constitute the entire Agreement. Facsimile signatures, as well as original signatures, shall be sufficient to evidence execution of the Agreement by any party hereto,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "6. Integration and written modification",
    "text": "6. All negotiations, considerations, representations and understandings between the parties are incorporated herein and may be modified or altered only by a memorandum in writing and signed by the parties."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "6. No continuing waiver",
    "text": "No waiver of condition or covenant of this Agreement by either party hereto shalt be deemed to comprise or constitute a future waiver by such party of the sume of any other condition or covenant,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "Exhibit A §1. Management fee",
    "text": "1. For Management, four percont (4%) of Gross Income collected from rents and other services and shall never include receipts or proceeds from a sale of the Buildings."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "Exhibit A §2. Additional-duty fee",
    "text": "2, If Principal requests Managing Agent to perform dutics not outtined in the Agreement, such as appealing Real Estate Tax Assessments, or other specific requests, Managing Agent shall be paid a fee mutually agreed upon by Principal and Managing Agent,"
  }
]

