{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c014",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Making \"any decisions\" of the designated representative \"binding on Principal\" is hard to reconcile with Paragraph 6, which permits modification or alteration of the Agreement only by a memorandum in writing signed by the parties. A court would have to decide whether the representative's oral approvals — including authorizations under Paragraph 2(d) — bind Principal notwithstanding the writing requirement.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The insurance obligation is fixed only as \"such reasonable amount as the Principal shall determine,\" which combines an objective reasonableness limit with unilateral discretion and states no coverage floor. Whether the Agent, as additional insured, can complain of an inadequate limit is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c016",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Cooperate in all matters\" and the Principal's right to \"designate general policies\" have no defined content or boundary, and the Agent's \"privilege and obligation of submitting recommendations\" carries no consequence. A court would have to decide what conduct breaches a duty pitched at that level of generality.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c017",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"[E]ither party may cancel this Agreement at the end of any calendar month after closing, upon not less than thirty (30) days' written notice\" does not say whether notice may be given before closing, whether the thirty days must expire before the chosen month-end, or how long after a sale the right survives. The timing mechanics of the cancellation right are ambiguous.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c018",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The clause both allows termination \"at any time upon thirty (30) days prior written notice\" and conditions it on a breach uncured within thirty days of a written notice, without saying whether one notice serves both functions or two are required. The trailing cap — an extended cure \"in any event never longer than 90 days\" — also leaves unstated what date the ninety days runs from.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.34}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c019",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Binding the Agreement on \"successors and assigns\" implies assignability, yet Paragraph 1 appoints Hokanson as \"exclusive representative, manager and agent\" in what is otherwise a personal-services engagement and no provision permits or conditions assignment. A court would have to decide whether the Agent may assign its management duties.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c020",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Prevailing party\" is undefined and the trigger — \"any dispute ... arising out of, related to or connected with this Agreement\" — is not limited to litigation, so it is unclear who prevails in a mixed or partial outcome and whether non-judicial disputes count. Both terms would require construction before fees could be awarded.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c021",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The counterparts sentence says the counterparts \"when taken together, shall constitute the entire Agreement,\" borrowing merger language into a signature-formalities clause, which sits uneasily with Paragraph 6's statement that all prior negotiations and understandings \"are incorporated herein.\" A court would have to decide whether either sentence operates as an integration clause.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c022",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Saying that all prior \"negotiations, considerations, representations and understandings ... are incorporated herein\" is ambiguous: it can be read as a merger clause superseding them, or, literally, as making unwritten prior understandings part of the contract. That choice determines whether extrinsic representations are enforceable terms.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.36}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c023",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The sentence is garbled — a waiver shall not \"comprise or constitute a future waiver by such party of the sume of any other condition or covenant\" — where \"comprise\" appears to be \"compromise\" and \"the sume of\" appears to be \"the same or.\" As written it is unclear whether the clause preserves rights as to the same covenant or only as to other covenants.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c024",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Gross Income collected from rents and other services\" is undefined: it does not say whether tenant reimbursements of operating expenses, security deposits, late fees, insurance or condemnation proceeds fall within it, and \"other services\" has no stated boundary. The single express carve-out for sale proceeds invites an expressio unius argument that everything else is included.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c025",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The extra fee is one \"mutually agreed upon by Principal and Managing Agent,\" with no rate, formula or fallback mechanism — an agreement to agree that gives a court nothing to enforce if the parties do not agree. Whether the Agent may refuse the requested duty or claim a reasonable fee is unstated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
     {"issue": "The category of \"duties not outlined in the Agreement\" cannot be fixed without Paragraph 2(a), which already requires the Agent to \"perform such other duties that are customarily performed by Managing Agents\" for the base management fee. A court would have to decide on which side of that line a requested service such as a tax-assessment appeal falls.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
   ]}
]}

